# Documentation
# Only CLAUDE.md, README.md, NEWS.md and the Claude Code team config (.claude/rules, .claude/commands)
# are committed. docs/ (architecture reference, decision log, authoring guides) stays local on purpose.
*.md
!CLAUDE.md
!/README.md
!/NEWS.md
!.claude/rules/*.md
!.claude/commands/*.md
docs/
.todo
.agents/

# Scripts - ignore all except those needed for GitHub Actions workflow
# (.github/workflows/sync-airtable.yml runs these; they must be in the repo)
#
# `scripts/*` not `scripts/`: excluding the directory itself stops git descending into it, and a
# negation cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded. With `scripts/` the
# rules below were inert — those files are in the repo only because they were committed before
# the rule existed, and any newly added workflow script would silently never be committed.
#
# Re-included by pattern, not one line per file: a per-file list has the same failure mode a
# rung down, because the next `sync_*` script is committed only if someone remembers to add a
# line here. A local-only `sync_*` script would now be picked up — but that shows up in
# `git status`, which is the loud failure, not the silent one.
scripts/*
!scripts/sync_*
!scripts/ensure_survey_indexes.cjs
# Claude Code (personal)
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
